>>
Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 2 (tensor dimensions must be at least 3)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3
>>
Rule 3 (positive upscale factor)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 > 0
>>
Rule 4 (input channel dimension divisible by square of upscale factor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= shape(v_1, -3) % (v_2 * v_2) = 0
